3 product_weight_g   -0.623    0.0393     -15.8 1.70e-56


In the simple numeric linear model (wf_lm_r1 on recipe_1, where predictors are normalized to mean 0 and SD 1), the intercept is about 12.01 days at average freight_value and product_weight_g. A 1-SD increase in freight_value is associated with roughly +2.41 more delivery days (\(p &lt; 2.2 \times 10^{-16}\)), whereas a 1-SD increase in product_weight_g has a small negative coefficient of about \(-0.62\) days (\(p = 1.70 \times 10^{-56}\)) once freight_value is held constant—reflecting the correlation between weight and freight cost seen earlier, as well as why simple two-feature linear models have limitations before adding geography, timing, and item details.



